            </div>
        </div>
        <div data-aos="fade-up" class="aos-init aos-animate">
            <div class="row">
                <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-3 mb-4">
                    <div class="card">
                        <h5 class="card-title">Fire Adequacy Survey</h5>
                        <p class="card-text">A Fire Adequacy Survey is a detailed evaluation designed to assess the fire safety readiness of a building or facility.</p>
                        <a href="@Url.Content("~/Home/firaadeqacysurvey")" class="arrow">
                            <i class="fas fa-long-arrow-alt-right"></i>
                        </a>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-3 mb-4">
                    <div class="card">
                        <h5 class="card-title">Fire Safety Audit</h5>
                        <p class="card-text">A Fire Safety Audit is a detailed evaluation of a facility’s fire safety measures, designed to ensure that systems, procedures, and equipment function effectively and comply with safety regulations.</p>
                        <a href="@Url.Content("~/Home/firesafetyauditfire")" class="arrow">
                            <i class="fas fa-long-arrow-alt-right"></i>
                        </a>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-3 mb-4">
                    <div class="card">
                        <h5 class="card-title">Fire Load Calculation</h5>
                        <p class="card-text">Fire load calculation is an essential process in fire safety engineering that measures the potential intensity of a fire within a specific area. This calculation evaluates the quantity and combustibility of all materials present, including furniture, equipment, and structural components, to estimate the heat energy that could be released during a fire.</p>
                        <a href="@Url.Content("~/Home/firaloadcalculation")" class="arrow">
                            <i class="fas fa-long-arrow-alt-right"></i>
                        </a>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-3 mb-4">
                    <div class="card">
                        <h5 class="card-title">Design of Fire Network</h5>
                        <p class="card-text">The design of a fire network is a critical element of fire safety planning, aimed at creating a robust system to detect, control, and suppress fires effectively. A well-designed fire network ensures that water or other extinguishing agents are delivered to the right locations with adequate pressure and flow, providing rapid response in case of an emergency.</p>
                        <a href="@Url.Content("~/Home/designofnetwork")" class="arrow">
                            <i class="fas fa-long-arrow-alt-right"></i>
                        </a>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

